WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.120
Hello !

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.000
Now that we're online,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.809
we know that a lot of you 
have been turning your

00:00:03.809 --> 00:00:05.530
cameras...off. 

00:00:05.794 --> 00:00:06.973
And we get it.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:10.715
You're online. You don't even 
have to change out of your hoodie,

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:13.600
and your jogging bottoms and your pyjamas.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.225
Wait my camera's on?!

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:17.027
 

00:00:17.027 --> 00:00:19.697
BUT, let me give you a&nbsp;
couple of reasons why

00:00:19.697 --> 00:00:22.231
you really need to 
keep your cameras on

00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:24.709
during your English 
lessons with&nbsp;us on Zoom.

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:25.439
You ready?

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:26.080
You ready?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.617
Number 1: help to avoid the 
English lesson from a horror story.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.500
Okay let me just paint
a picture for you.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.564
Imagine for one second, you 
are your English teacher.

00:00:37.564 --> 00:00:38.837
Good morning everybody!

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:40.320
How are you doing today?

00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:45.890
Okay, well, 

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:46.974
I know it's early.

00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:51.569
I'm&nbsp;going to need you all to make 
an effort to practise your speaking.

00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:54.957
Sophia, how&nbsp;did you find
this week's homework?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.431
Can you imagine presenting a 
project under&nbsp;those circumstances?

00:01:00.431 --> 00:01:04.078
Our teacher here is in a little 
bit of a difficult situation.

00:01:04.078 --> 00:01:09.689
It's really difficult to teach 
to muted, black, squares.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:13.686
It's also very important&nbsp;that you can see your classmates faces, 

00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:17.466
so that you can connect and feel like you're&nbsp;in a real classroom.

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:22.105
Having your camera on will make you feel a 
lot more confident when speaking&nbsp;English.

00:01:22.105 --> 00:01:23.792
So turn those cameras on!

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:27.177
Number 2: help yourself 
with pronunciation.

00:01:27.177 --> 00:01:29.541
Let's just go&nbsp;back to our English
teacher for one second.

00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:30.608
Okay Sophia.

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:32.653
Could you repeat after&nbsp;me please?

00:01:32.653 --> 00:01:37.428
I can see 13 sheep through the window.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.871
Let's try the word&nbsp;sheep again.

00:01:42.871 --> 00:01:45.000
Really elongate those "e's".

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.965
"eeeeeee"

00:01:47.484 --> 00:01:48.594
"ee"

00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:49.748
"sheeeeep"

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:53.586
"eee?"

00:01:53.586 --> 00:01:56.526
Our teachers can really help
you with your&nbsp;pronunciation,

00:01:56.526 --> 00:01:57.920
if they can see you.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.039
Non-verbal communication.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:02.607
We use it every single day.

00:02:02.607 --> 00:02:06.711
If&nbsp;facial expressions and body language 
make up 70% of communication

00:02:06.711 --> 00:02:08.083
when we're offline.

00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:11.452
We&nbsp;definitely need to be using 
them when we're online.

00:02:11.452 --> 00:02:13.733
So turn those cameras on! 

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:18.675
Number 3: stop&nbsp;strangers from
Zoom bombing your classroom.

00:02:18.675 --> 00:02:20.659
Okay, this might sound obvious,

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:22.514
but this person&nbsp;

00:02:23.687 --> 00:02:26.739
is a lot easier to spot than this person.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.889
Yes, at the British Council we do everything

00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:34.130
to ensure only you and your classmates 

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.829
are allowed into your classroom.

00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:38.173
But you can never&nbsp;be too careful.

00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:40.755
We want you to be safe whilst
learning English with us.

00:02:40.755 --> 00:02:44.323
Your parents want you&nbsp;to be safe 
whilst learning English with us.

00:02:44.323 --> 00:02:47.525
I'm assuming you want you to be safe 
whilst learning&nbsp;English with us.

00:02:47.525 --> 00:02:50.820
Help us detect strangers
trying to enter your classroom

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.123
by turning your&nbsp;cameras on.

00:02:53.123 --> 00:02:55.230
Okay, I hope I've made my point.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.826
Please, please, please, please, please, please,

00:02:57.826 --> 00:03:00.000
turn&nbsp;your cameras on!

00:03:00.228 --> 00:03:00.886
What?

00:03:00.886 --> 00:03:02.300
Turn those cameras ON.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.615
You'll have a lot more fun,

00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:05.670
your teachers will have a&nbsp;
lot more fun

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.767
and just generally it will be a much more enjoyable 

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.146
experience for everybody involved.

00:03:11.146 --> 00:03:13.805
Okay that's everything from me.
For today.

00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:14.701
Bye! 

